Solution:
It may help to rewrite f(x) = [\cos (2 x)]^{7}. Use the Chain Rule with inside function u = \cos (2 x) and outside function y = u^{7}. A second application of Chain Rule is used to find \frac{du}{dx}.
\begin{array}{rcl} f'(x) \amp =\amp \displaystyle\frac{dy}{du} \cdot \frac{du}{dx}\\ \amp \amp \\ \amp =\amp (7 u^{6})(-\sin(2 x) \cdot 2) \\ \amp =\amp -14 \cos^{6}(2 x)\sin(2 x) \end{array}
